  "summary": "Meme Man floats through non-Euclidean dread: humor after meaning broke.",
  "description": "Surreal memes are the internet's absurdism proper: Meme Man (the smooth 3D head), geometric beings, impossible spaces, distorted typography (\"stonks\", \"succ\") and non-Euclidean dread rendered in bad-CGI and dream logic. Emerging mid-2010s from Tumblr and Reddit (r/surrealmemes, 2015+), the genre replaced relatable humor with dimensional wrongness — comedy for a generation fluent in post-irony. Its visual toolkit (bad renders, stock-corpse 3D objects, unicode mangling, cosmic voids) influenced glitch art, vaporwave's weirder cousins and the \"weirdcore/dreamcore\" family, while Meme Man became one of the internet's central mascots.",
  "culturalContext": "Surreal memes are the internet's absurdism proper: Meme Man and dimensional wrongness replaced relatable humor with post-irony, the genre fed weirdcore and glitch aesthetics, and \"stonks\" proved surrealism could be a universal meme language.",
